 "verdict": "No data-side hole in the corpus: all 33,429 six-metal complexes carry geometry, Wiberg bond truth and NBO charges, with one metal atom each and a metal column that agrees with it everywhere. The split is scaffold-disjoint (0 spanning scaffolds) but allocates 87.7/6.2/6.2 % of rows, because the fractions are budgeted in scaffold counts; tmqm_val_frac is ignored on that branch. The 192-cloud val cohort every generation metric is averaged over is Pt 19 / Ru 93 at seed 0, against a corpus that is Pt 24.8 % / Ru 29.3 %: Pt is present but 2.5x under-weighted. Raising tmqm_min_per_metal to 20 balances it (Pt 46 / Ru 52) and forces a full 2,061-candidate scan instead of a 960-candidate window.",
